Create a snapshot from a specified l_ssd volume.

USAGE:
  scw instance snapshot create [arg=value ...]

EXAMPLES:
  Create a snapshot in the default zone from a specified volume ID
    scw instance snapshot create base-volume-id=11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111

  Create a snapshot in fr-par-1 zone from a specified volume ID
    scw instance snapshot create zone=fr-par-1 base-volume-id=11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111

  Create a named snapshot from a specified volume ID
    scw instance snapshot create name=foobar base-volume-id=11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111

ARGS:
  [project-id]         Project ID to use. If none is passed the default project ID will be used
  [name=<generated>]   Name of the snapshot
  [tags.{index}]       Tags associated with the snapshot
  [base-volume-id]     ID of the base volume
  [public]             Whether the snapshot should be public
  [zone=fr-par-1]      Zone to target. If none is passed will use default zone from the config (fr-par-1 | fr-par-2 | fr-par-3 | nl-ams-1 | nl-ams-2 | nl-ams-3 | pl-waw-1 | pl-waw-2 | pl-waw-3 | it-mil-1)

DEPRECATED ARGS:
  [volume-id]   ID of the base volume, please use base-volume-id instead

FLAGS:
  -h, --help[=true|false]                help for create
      --list-sub-commands[=true|false]   List all subcommands
  -w, --wait[=true|false]                wait until the snapshot is ready

GLOBAL FLAGS:
  -B, --beta[=true|false]         Enable beta mode
  -c, --config string             The path to the config file
  -D, --debug[=true|false]        Enable debug mode
  -H, --no-headers[=true|false]   Skip headers in human output
  -o, --output string             Output format: json or human, see 'scw help output' for more info (default "human")
  -p, --profile string            The config profile to use
      --web[=true|false]          open console page for the current resource
